17	 *
18	 * Three things about the merged workflow are easy to lose in an edit and expensive
19	 * to lose in production, so they are pinned here rather than left to a reader:
20	 *
21	 * - the jobs are chained by `needs`, and `apply-to-self` names BOTH of its
22	 *   predecessors, because the tag it announces is `release`'s output and GitHub
23	 *   exposes outputs only to a job that names their job directly;
